1. Definitions. "GÉNESIS" or "the Program" is the GÉNESIS desktop application, its
   updates, code, design, graphic and sound assets, texts, catalogs and
   documentation. "Author" is SystemOrlando · Brakescode. "You" is the person or
   organization installing or using the Program. "Official page" is the
   downloads section of https://github.com/SystemOrlando/genesis-app.

2. Ownership. The Program belongs to the Author and is protected by copyright and
   intellectual-property laws. It is licensed, not sold.

3. What you may do. The Author grants you a personal, non-exclusive,
   non-transferable, revocable license to: (a) install and use the Program, on
   Windows or Linux, on computers you control, for your own personal or your
   organization's internal purposes; (b) keep one backup copy of the installer
   you downloaded from the official page; (c) receive and apply the updates the
   Program offers; (d) use what the Program produces for you as you wish, subject
   to the terms of the AI engines and services you connected.

4. What you may not do. Without the Author's written permission, you may not:
   (a) decompile, disassemble or reverse engineer the Program or try to obtain its
   source code, except to the strict extent mandatory law allows despite this
   prohibition; (b) copy, redistribute, resell, rent, lend, sublicense or make the
   Program or parts of it available to third parties, or offer it as a service;
   (c) modify it or create derivative works for distribution; (d) use its code,
   design, texts or any part of it to train, fine-tune or evaluate artificial
   intelligence models, or include it in datasets for that purpose; (e) remove or
   alter authorship, trademark or license notices; (f) circumvent, disable or
   remove its technical protections (obfuscation, update signature checks) or
   extract its assets from the installer for use outside GÉNESIS; (g) publish or
   share the installer outside the official page; (h) use the Program to harm
   others, to access systems without permission, or for any unlawful purpose.

5. Third-party components. GÉNESIS uses open-source components, each under its own
   license (e.g. MIT, Apache-2.0, BSD, MPL-2.0, OFL), which prevail for those
   components; the list is in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md. GÉNESIS may install, open
   or connect to third-party programs and services (AI engines, local models,
   voices, connectors, web services); they are not part of the installer, and
   your use of them is governed by their own terms. Third-party names and logos
   belong to their owners and imply no affiliation or endorsement.

6. Your responsibility when using an agent. GÉNESIS can act on your computer and
   services with the permissions you give it. You give the orders and choose the
   control level, protected paths and blocked apps. The Guidelines reduce risk but
   do not remove it. You are responsible for reviewing what you ask and what it
   does, for keeping backups of what matters, and for using the Program lawfully
   and in line with the terms of the services you connect.

7. Data and privacy. Your files, conversations and memory stay on your computer;
   keys and credentials are kept in your system's credential store. GÉNESIS sends
   over the internet only what is needed for what you ask: to the AI engine you
   choose, to the services you connect, to GitHub to check for updates and the
   connector catalog, and the feedback messages you write and send. The Author
   does not receive your files, conversations or keys. Details are in the "Before
   you start" documents inside the app.

8. Trademarks. "GÉNESIS", "Brakescode" and their logos are the Author's marks. You
   may not use them in a way that suggests endorsement or affiliation, except to
   refer to the Program truthfully.

9. Updates. The Program checks for new versions and notifies you; it installs them
   when you confirm, and only if signed by the Author. Each update is governed by
   this license or by the most recent version accompanying it. If you disagree
   with a new version of the license, stop using the Program.

10. Beta. While GÉNESIS is distributed as "beta": (a) it is a test version that may
    have bugs, lose the app's own data or stop working; do not use it as the only
    copy of important information or for critical tasks; (b) the Author may
    change, limit or end the beta at any time; (c) feedback you send may be used
    freely to improve GÉNESIS, without payment or attribution; only what you
    write (and, if you opt in, app version, OS and engine) is sent, never your
    files, conversations or keys; (d) the Linux version is newer and less tested
    than the Windows one.

11. No warranty; limitation of liability. The Program is provided "as is" and "as
    available", without warranty of any kind, express or implied, including
    merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose and non-infringement. An AI
    agent's output may be wrong, incomplete or unexpected, and is not professional
    advice. To the extent the law allows, the Author is not liable for indirect
    damages or loss of data, revenue or opportunities arising from use or
    inability to use the Program. Nothing here excludes or limits what the law does
    not allow to be excluded or limited, or your non-waivable consumer rights.

12. Termination. This license ends automatically if you breach any of its terms.
    You may end it by ceasing to use the Program and deleting your copies. Upon
    termination you must stop using the Program and delete your copies. Sections
    2, 4, 8, 11 and 13 survive.

13. General. If a part of this license cannot be enforced, the rest remains in
    force. Failure to enforce a condition is not a waiver. This license, together
    with the in-app "Before you start" documents, is the entire agreement about
    the Program. You may not assign it without the Author's written permission.

14. Contact: contacto@brakescode.com
